      "content": "Soil pH between 5.5 and 7.0 is the optimal range for grapevines, as it prevents the immobility and toxicity of essential micronutrients like iron and manganese. Below this slightly acidic threshold, iron and manganese become increasingly available, which can trigger chlorosis and oxidative stress if levels exceed vine capacity. Conversely, maintaining pH within or near 6.0 ensures a balanced solubility profile where these nutrients remain accessible without risking deficiency or saturation. This stable environment supports efficient uptake, critical for vine nutrition and fruit quality in Central Valley soils.",
